ABSTRACT<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>Line spectra radiated by moving targets are important features for passive sonar detection and classification. Relative motion between a target and the receiver induces time\u2010varying Doppler shifts in the received line spectra, causing phase misalignment during long\u2010time Fourier integration and resulting in spectral broadening, energy dispersion and coherent integration loss. To address this problem, this paper proposes a matched frequency\u2010trajectory estimation method for long\u2010time coherent integration enhancement (MFT\u2010LTCIE). The method transforms the received signal into its analytic representation, extracts the narrowband component around the target line spectrum and partitions the signal into short\u2010time segments. For each segment, matching responses are computed over a candidate frequency grid, and a maximum\u2010matching criterion is used to estimate the segment\u2010wise frequency trajectory. The estimated trajectory is interpolated onto the sample\u2010time axis and used to construct a phase\u2010compensation function relative to a reference frequency. Trajectory\u2010guided phase compensation restores phase coherence, and a full\u2010duration FFT of the compensated signal yields an enhanced coherent integration spectrum. Simulations show that MFT\u2010LTCIE suppresses Doppler\u2010induced spectral broadening and maintains sharp spectral peaks under different signal\u2010to\u2010noise ratios and target speeds. Experimental ship\u2010radiated noise data further demonstrate its ability to track line\u2010spectrum variations and refocus dispersed energy.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1049\/rsn2.70216","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,4]],"date-time":"2026-08-04T21:41:18Z","timestamp":1785879678000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Long\u2010Time Coherent Integration Enhancement of Moving Target Line Spectrum Based on Matched Frequency\u2010Trajectory Estimation"],"prefix":"10.1049","volume":"20","author":[{"given":"Yushu","family":"Zhang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Marine Technology Ocean University of China  Qingdao China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0006-0684-2999","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Zhenxing","family":"Zhao","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Marine Technology Ocean University of China  Qingdao China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Lin","family":"Zhai","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Marine Technology Ocean University of China  Qingdao China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Bo","family":"Gao","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Marine Technology Ocean University of China  Qingdao China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Dazhi","family":"Gao","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Marine Technology Ocean University of China  Qingdao China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Wei","family":"Gao","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Marine Technology Ocean University of China  Qingdao China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"265","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,4]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_12_2_1","volume-title":"Principles of Underwater Sound","author":"Urick R. J.","year":"1983"},{"key":"e_1_2_12_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.3354\/meps08353"},{"key":"e_1_2_12_4_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1109\/TAU.1967.1161901"},{"key":"e_1_2_12_5_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1109\/5.30749"},{"key":"e_1_2_12_6_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.apacoust.2009.08.007"},{"key":"e_1_2_12_7_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DO